+           including any conversion and compression, but into memory, so that
+           nothing is written to disk, no file is created, and a file object
+           passed as ``fp`` is left untouched. Errors the writer would raise,
+           such as an unsupported mode for the format, are still raised. Whether
+           the file could be opened for writing, for example whether its
